<title>MALAYSIA: Esprit requests suspension continuation.</title>
<headline>Esprit requests suspension continuation.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian construction company Esprit Group Bhd on Tuesday asked the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange to continue the suspension of its shares.</p>
<p>Esprit said the &quot;negotiation in respect of material transaction involving the company... is still pending&quot;.</p>
<p>No other details were given.</p>
<p>Esprit was last traded on June 4, when it closed at 11 ringgit.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-206 2323)</p>
</text>
